Status Meaning Content type Schema <code>201</code> Successful response <code>application/json</code> <code>ServiceEnvironmentMutationResponse</code> <code>409</code> Conflict. <code>WORKER_REVOKED</code> (<code>details.workerId</code>): with <code>assignedWorkerId</code>, that Worker is revoked; revoked is terminal (enroll a new Worker or replace the revoked one), so the refusal is stored against the Idempotency-Key and replays. Without <code>assignedWorkerId</code>, the Worker selection chose (the project default or automatic placement) was revoked before the placement locked it; that refusal is not stored against the key, so a retry with the same key selects again. <code>NO_ELIGIBLE_WORKER</code> (<code>details.requiredCapabilities</code>, <code>details.defaultWorkerId</code>): no Worker is eligible, or the Worker placement chose was removed, replaced or became ineligible after the request's pre-check, including a removed or replaced project default. Placement does not reselect, but the refusal is not stored against the key, so a retry with the same key selects again. <code>WORKER_UPGRADE_REQUIRED</code>: with <code>assignedWorkerId</code>, that Worker does not advertise a capability the operation needs (<code>details.workerId</code>, <code>details.requiredCapability</code>); without it, the project default or automatic candidate runs a version below the one the control plane expects (<code>details.requiredCapabilities</code>). Upgrade the Worker and retry; the refusal is not stored against the key, so a retry with the same key runs again. <code>404</code> <code>NOT_FOUND</code> applies only to an explicit <code>assignedWorkerId</code> already removed or replaced when the request arrived, including one that is also revoked. Other conflicts on this route also use this status. <code>application/json</code> <code>ErrorResponse</code> <code>default</code> Error <code>application/json</code> <code>ErrorResponse</code> <p>Illustrative success body:</p> <pre><code>{
